      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "We want to solve E to the power seven point five K equals two. Why take L N, rather than log base ten.",
          "asks": ["What is L N?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 0 }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b1.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b1.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Both logs bring the power down. With log base ten, we get seven point five K, times log E, equals log two.",
          "asks": ["Why does the power come down?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 1, "on": "With log base ten" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b2.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b2.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "But log E is an awkward number, about zero point four three four. It stays in the working.",
          "asks": ["What is log of e?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 2, "on": "log E is an awkward number" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b3.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b3.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "L N is log base E. With L N, we get seven point five K, times L N E, equals L N two.",
          "asks": ["What does base e mean?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 3, "on": "With L N, we get" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b4.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b4.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "And L N E is exactly one, because E to the power one is E.",
          "asks": ["Why is L N E equal to 1?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 4, "on": "is exactly one" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b5.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b5.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "So the L N E simply leaves the working: seven point five K equals L N two.",
          "asks": ["Do both ways give the same K?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 5, "on": "seven point five K equals" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b6.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/why-ln-when-e-am/scene-01-b6.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Both ways give the same K. L N is just neater, because L N E is one.",
          "asks": ["When do I use log base ten?"],
